 "final_result": "Built a three-script Python workflow for cubic perovskite CsPbBr3 (mp-600089, Pm-3m #221) from scratch.\n\nWORKFLOW:\n1. Fetched base CsPbBr3 CIF from Materials Project (mp-600089, Pm-3m #221). The cell already had 5 atoms (Cs1, Pb1, Br3) -- already primitive. Saved to structures/primitive_CsPbBr3.cif.\n2. generate_structures.py: Generated 51 structures (structure_000.cif through structure_050.cif) with random atomic displacements (T=400 K, cubic phase stable above ~320 K) and small random lattice strain. RMS displacements: Cs=0.381 A, Pb=0.168 A, Br=0.129 A (lighter/weakly bound atoms move more).\n3. Fetched fully relativistic (fr) Pseudo-Dojo pseudopotentials (pbesol, stringent, nc, upf) for Cs (z_valence=9), Pb (z_valence=22), Br (z_valence=17). Total electrons = 82.\n4. setup_jobs.py: Created calculations/NNN/ for all 51 structures with pw.in (SCF), bands.in (NSCF bands), bands_post.in (bands.x), kpath.json, and pseudopotential files. Key settings: ecutwfc=88 Ry (Pb: 44 Ha * 2), ecutrho=352 Ry, nbnd=128, noncolin=.true., lspinorb=.true., occupations='fixed', conv_thr=1e-8, SCF kpts=(4,4,4).\n5. Ran run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000 -- all three steps (scf, bands_scf, bands_post) completed successfully.\n6. plot_bands.py: Parsed 000.bands.dat, aligned to VBM (82 occupied bands with SOC), plotted band structure with proper k-path labels and ticks, saved to calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nRESULTS:\n- VBM: 4.591 eV (shifted to 0)\n- CBM: 0.373 eV (relative to VBM)\n- Band gap: 0.373 eV\n\nASE FUNCTIONS USED:\n- ase.io.read/write for CIF I/O\n- ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in for pw.x input files\n- chem_llm.kpath (standard_kpath, kp_atoms, kp_kpts, kp_save, plot_axis) for k-path and plotting\n\nSCIENTIFIC ASSUMPTIONS:\n- T=400 K chosen because cubic CsPbBr3 is stable above ~320 K (room temperature is below the orthorhombic-to-cubic transition)\n- Fully relativistic pseudopotentials with spin-orbit coupling (Cs Z=55, Pb Z=82 are post-Xe)\n- occupations='fixed' (semiconductor with ~1.78 eV experimental gap)\n- ecutwfc=88 Ry (max of all three elements, Pb highest)\n\nEXPERT REVIEW NEEDED:\n- The DFT band gap (0.373 eV) is significantly smaller than the experimental value (~1.78 eV) -- this is expected for PBE/PBESOL functionals which underestimate band gaps. A hybrid functional (HSE06) or GW calculation would be needed for quantitative agreement.\n- The 4x4x4 k-point mesh for SCF may be slightly coarse for a 5.95 A cubic cell; a 6x6x6 or 8x8x8 mesh could be considered for higher accuracy.",
